Dear Records Custodian:

Pursuant to the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA), 45 C.F.R.
§ 164.508, and the enclosed Authorization for Release of Protected Health Information
executed by {{ plaintiff_name }}, we hereby request the following records from your
facility:

1.  PRE-ACCIDENT MEDICAL RECORDS — All records for {{ plaintiff_name }} for the period
    {{ pre_existing_start }} through {{ pre_existing_end }}, including:

    (a) Records relating to any treatment of the spine, neck (cervical), lower back,
        or lower extremities (including knees), including: intake documentation,
        progress notes, diagnostic imaging, and discharge summaries;

    (b) Records relating to any head injury, concussion, or neurological complaint,
        including: evaluation notes, imaging, and follow-up documentation;

    (c) Any notation in the record of prior accidents, trauma, or injuries relevant
        to the above body regions.

2.  SCOPE NOTE — This request is limited to records relevant to the body regions
    identified above. We do not request records for conditions unrelated to the
    musculoskeletal or neurological systems.

This request is made in connection with a personal injury claim arising from an accident
that occurred on {{ incident_date }}. These pre-accident records are sought to provide
a complete medical history for {{ plaintiff_name }} and to document the baseline
condition of the affected body regions prior to the accident.

Please produce the requested records within thirty (30) days of receipt of this letter.
If a fee for reproduction is required, please advise our office in writing before
processing, and we will authorize payment.

